South African conservationists say  they're waging a war against poachers  and Anton mzimba was one of the many  Park Rangers on the front line he  dedicated his career to protecting  Wildlife it's very painful to see how  cruel people are it was Anton's success  as head Ranger at Timber Valley private  nature reserve for more than two decades  that cost him his life for months and  years Anton had been targeted receiving  death threats his family was receiving  threats his team was receiving threats  he was under a huge amount of pressure  Matt lindenberg was making a documentary  about Anton titled Rhino man but in July  before it was released his friend was  fatally shot  three men approached Anton's home under  the guise of needing water for their  vehicle they took weapons out and  unloaded on him  and in the process injured his wife and  also I think the most devastating thing  just to show how violent this  this war and poaching is is they took  shots at his children Anton leaves  behind seven children his wife survived  the attack I saw the blood I saw how he  was shot I saw the kids  it was just it was just  difficult it was too much Anton's cousin  Leyton Cabela is also a park ranger with  the all-female group The Black Mambas  she knows every time she puts on her  boots she's walking into Danger  it's not easy to wake up every day go  out on patrol  I'm doing this for him I'm doing this  for his legacy  the numbers of rhinos in Kruger National  Park have declined so much that poachers  are now turning their attention to  private reserves and it's up to those  landowners to foot the bill for extra  security measures to protect these  animals the same animals the government  promotes as one of its greatest tourist  attractions okay Reserve owner Derek  leverton supplies his ranges with body  armor and night vision goggles to help  keep them safe what these syndicates  will do to families to get their hands  on horn is frightening he's also applied  for a gun license  the teams that come poach they'll bring  one gun for the Rhinos they'll bring two  guns for us  it is very risky no arrests have been  made in connection with Anton's murder  as well as Wildlife Anton also had a  passion for teaching young people about  conservation she said you know if our  children if my children don't see the  value the beauty if they don't even have  empathy care compassion understanding  for wildlife how can I expect them to  protect that Wildlife Matt is helping to  continue Anton's Legacy and while the  film's ending has changed its message  has not  Emily anguin Al Jazeera Hood Sprite  South Africa
 

